What was the bug?
When a student places an order, the browser generates an order and registers it with the device's member ID (X-Member-Id). However, navigating to the "My Orders" section displayed:
  Where was the bug located?
File: backend/routes/orders.routes.js
Endpoint: GET /api/orders (lines 181–204)
  When the frontend fetches orders for the current user, it calls:

// frontend/js/orders.js (line 132)
const data = await api.listOrders({ memberId: deviceId(), limit: 25 });
// Requests: GET /api/orders?memberId=m-xxxxxx&limit=25

Notice that the query parameter sent by the client is named memberId.
However, in backend/routes/orders.routes.js at line 188:

// BEFORE (Buggy code):
if (req.query.status) orders = orders.filter((o) => o.status === req.query.status);
if (req.query.memberId) orders = orders.filter((o) => o.memberId === req.query.userId);
if (req.query.active === 'true') { ... }

It checked if (req.query.memberId) (which was true).
But it filtered with o.memberId === req.query.userId.
Because req.query.userId was never sent by the frontend, req.query.userId was undefined.
The comparison o.memberId === undefined evaluated to false for every single order.
As a result, every order was filtered out and an empty list [] was returned to the browser!

  The Fix in Detail
In backend/routes/orders.routes.js, line 188 was updated to check req.query.memberId (with fallback to req.query.userId):

  --- a/backend/routes/orders.routes.js
+++ b/backend/routes/orders.routes.js
@@ -185,7 +185,8 @@ router.get(
     let orders = all.slice();
 
     if (req.query.status) orders = orders.filter((o) => o.status === req.query.status);
-    if (req.query.memberId) orders = orders.filter((o) => o.memberId === req.query.userId);
+    const memberId = req.query.memberId || req.query.userId;
+    if (memberId) orders = orders.filter((o) => o.memberId === memberId);
     if (req.query.active === 'true') {
       orders = orders.filter((o) => !statusLogic.TERMINAL.includes(o.status));
     }
